cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Simple dynamic pricing rules versus a tuned fixed price for a perishable stock: a preregistered simulation study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kefi
    given-names: Mohamed Bechir
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: 0.1.0-rc1
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamedbechirkefi/fare-dynamic-pricing"
abstract: "FARE. Release candidate prepared for the owner's review, not released. A preregistered, reproducible simulation study of fixed, occupancy-based and demand-responsive pricing for perishable inventory (protocols frozen 2026-11-24; confirmatory runs complete; static offline demo built). At the base scenario the two dynamic rules earn +3.47% and +3.94% more than a tuned fixed price; across 9 market cells 8 of 18 contrasts are negative, including every loose-capacity cell, so no general advantage is supported. All results are simulated; the manuscript is a preprint draft, not peer-reviewed. Developed with an AI research and development assistant (Claude Code), which is not an author."
keywords:
  - dynamic pricing
  - revenue management
  - perishable inventory
  - simulation
